        "## 21.17 Python example: sequence entropy for a bigram model\n",
        "\n",
        "For a bigram Markov chain, conditional entropy is computed row by row.\n",
        "If $P$ is a transition matrix and $\\pi$ is the stationary or empirical distribution over previous tokens, then\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "H(W_t\\mid W_{t-1})=\\sum_i \\pi_i H(P_{i,\\cdot}).\n",
        "$$"
      ],
      "id": "475c1d2a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "\n",
        "vocab = [\"<s>\", \"the\", \"model\", \"learns\"]\n",
        "P = np.array([\n",
        "    [0.00, 0.70, 0.20, 0.10],\n",
        "    [0.00, 0.05, 0.80, 0.15],\n",
        "    [0.00, 0.10, 0.10, 0.80],\n",
        "    [0.00, 0.60, 0.20, 0.20]\n",
        "])\n",
        "pi = np.array([0.10, 0.35, 0.30, 0.25])\n",
        "\n",
        "def row_entropy(row):\n",
        "    positive = row[row > 0]\n",
        "    return -np.sum(positive * np.log(positive))\n",
        "\n",
        "row_entropies = np.array([row_entropy(row) for row in P])\n",
        "conditional_entropy = np.sum(pi * row_entropies)\n",
        "\n",
        "for word, h in zip(vocab, row_entropies):\n",
        "    print(f\"H(next | {word:6s}) = {h:.4f} nats\")\n",
        "print(\"Average conditional entropy:\", round(conditional_entropy, 4))\n",
        "print(\"Conditional perplexity:\", round(np.exp(conditional_entropy), 4))"
